    {"name": "Enterprise, 20 million a month, half of it released on chain, 100 lookups a month", "in": {"plan": "enterprise", "evaluations": 1000000, "accepted": "240000000.00", "on_chain_percent": 50, "lookups": 100}, "how": "Meter 900,000 x 0.002 x 12 = 21,600. A month's 20,000,000 at the volume rates: 3,000 + 19,000,000 x 0.20% = 41,000. The 10,000,000 released on chain lies first: 3,000 + 18,000 = 21,000 at the volume rates, and it paid 30,000 on chain, so 9,000 a month is rebated: 108,000 a year. The 10,000,000 reconciled off chain lies above it: 20,000 a month, 240,000 a year. Lookups 100 x 0.10 x 12 = 120. 400,000 + 21,600 + 240,000 + 120 - 108,000 = 553,720.", "out": {"control": "400,000.00", "meter": "21,600.00", "acceptance": "240,000.00", "paid_on_chain": "360,000.00", "rebate": "108,000.00", "records": "120.00", "total": "553,720.00", "benefit_to_demand": "1,661,160.00"}},
    {"name": "everything released on chain: the fee was paid there and is never on the invoice", "in": {"plan": "business", "evaluations": 0, "accepted": "6000000.00", "on_chain_percent": 100, "lookups": 0}, "how": "6,000,000 x 0.30% = 18,000 was paid to the program at release. 500,000 a month earns no volume rate. The invoice is Control.", "out": {"control": "100,000.00", "meter": "0.00", "acceptance": "0.00", "paid_on_chain": "18,000.00", "rebate": "0.00", "records": "0.00", "total": "100,000.00", "benefit_to_demand": "300,000.00"}},
